# Query bounded human tasks with scoped summaries

Local implementation verified at 0.3.0-dev.9. Deployment is unverified; set base_url (including /api/v1) only after checking the target release. No agent-runtime endpoints are included.

Current OPEN project membership is sufficient. Filters, counts and current public assignee identities share one page snapshot; no execution content or private profile lookup. Default50/max100, highest priority/newest creation first. Exact deadline sorting puts timed values first by pinned instant, then date-only by calendar date, unset last. Direction applies within each bucket. Existing deadlineDate calendar comparator and array list remain compatible. Generation changes return409 on continuation; refresh. Public names/lifecycle are current per-page display metadata and do not advance task query generation.

Authorization uses current effective permission keys plus resource scope and lifecycle checks. Role labels do not replace these checks.

This is a request template, not a captured successful execution. Replace placeholders and read conditional field rules before sending. Do not run a whole collection against live data: mutations may change files, credentials or execution state. No requests were executed as part of this documentation update.

Missing fields/defaults are not invented. Optional request fields are omitted in the starter body; the full field contract is below. Preserve UUID and original revision for documented idempotent retries. Confirm actual outcomes before generating a new command.

